# This test allocates until allocation fails: its array has a getter at index 0 that constructs a
# Uint8Array over the same array, which re-enters the getter, so each level maps another ~80MB, and
# index 80000000 sets the length. Those large allocations drain the primitive Gigacage's reserved
# region, and freeing them returns the memory to the large heap's free list rather than to the region.
# The region is handed to pas_reserved_memory_provider once at construction and never refilled --
# its config carries null_aligned_allocator, and pas_megapage_cache carries deallocator = NULL -- so
# once drained it cannot be replenished. Measured at the refusal: entries=2 total_free=12337152
# against a 16777216 request. Every later size class that needs a fresh 16MB megapage then fails for
# the life of the driver process, which is how this test's collateral reaches unrelated tests that run
# after it. Upstream records the same test as a flaky timeout on mac, ios and gtk
